{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/670097-how-to-cast-something-into-verse","id":670097,"title":"how to Cast something into verse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-18T13:33:44-07:00","id":670097,"title":"how to Cast something into verse?","content":"One problem I have with WTA sometimes is at moots and such giving stirring ballads about great deeds<br /> <br /> thought we could all come up with stories, and help each other cast it into verse.<br /> <br /> Heres my start<br /> <br /> sometime long ago a great garou heroine attacked a pair of leeches, one held her off urging the other to flee, and was destroyed... she saw nobility in his sacrafice. and so spared the other leech, out of respect to that selfless act<br /> <br /> Years latter her Sept, was attacked and destroyed by the leech that she spared in vengeance.<br /> <br /> &quot;Because a thing has many layers/Hidden facets, Hidden depths, does not make the first impression wrong&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:55:58-07:00","id":670250,"title":"","content":"English is not my native language so I don't feel qualified to help out with actual verse. Just a general tip: If you run into this problem more often, read some epic poetry and drama as your next book, and after a while you'll practically start to think in that rhythm. At least back in school after we were through with the German classics (Goethe, Schiller) that was my experience. ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:48:43-07:00","id":670347,"title":"","content":"Depending on the tribal background of the gallard in question it doesn't have to be in verse presay. A Get might put in it powerful spoken word while a bonegnawer might have it as a blues song and don't get me started on glasswalker dub steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:04:06-07:00","id":670449,"title":"","content":"I played a Shadow Lord Galliard who was a punk rocker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:45:43-07:00","id":671535,"title":"","content":"Back to topic....<br /> <br /> I once created a story for a Children of Gaia / Fianna sept at the border of Germany and the Czech Republic. It was about couple who didn't have, and couldn't get kids of their own - and were sad about it. They claimed a orphan garou cub that was found by the sept. They raised it as their own child and according to Fianna and sept tradition, the child gained a uncle/mentor, who shared some personality traits with the child - most prominently being reasonable and relatively unemotional (compared to the other Fianna).<br /> But, when the child had very well grown into adulthood and had gained rank and status, his adoptive parents died and the garou bid farewell to the sept, after coming to realise, how different he was to the people living there and that it was just the obligation towards and love for his parents that had kept him there.<br /> Decades later, the sept got word that their former sept made ruled with iron first over an area couple of weeks south from the sept's hunting grounds. So, the former mentor went to investigate. And, once he had reached and spoken to his former ward, he realised that he was of Shadowlord blood, but that all his ambition and drive had been left unfocused and ultimately led to the garou becoming a tyrant. The mentor challenged, fought and killed his former ward and returned home, where he told the story, declared his failure as mentor and disillusioned took the silver dagger into the woods...<br /> <br /> In the sept this story from the Dark ages or classical antiquity (people aren't sure) led to the sept's strict feeling about the need for cubs to be raised in an sept compromised of, and living by the traditions of, the tribe the cub belongs to though his/her blood. They barely tolerate rover packs or mixed septs to educate cubs if members of the cub's tribe live there - and they will take cubs not educated by garou of their heritage and see that they are brought into a sept that lives by the cub's tribe's traditions.<br /> <br /> The story also is a reminder of the fact, that being part of the tribe is a birthright and it gives each member of the sept great comfort, that they know that they will succeed in tasks associated with their tribe, simply because it is in their blood. Rarely a garou in this sept has self-doubt about any task that is something their tribe usually does.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, the responsibility for what mortals do lies with the mortals. The Shadow Lords cub could pass all requirements to get a Rite of Passage as Fianna and succeeded. Stag didn't veto - if simply to teach his children a lesson some decades later. Garou have responsibilities and they aren't easily diverted to their divine patrons (or any other spirit, or the ST, for that matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-19-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T23:13:47-07:00","id":672944,"title":"","content":"I tend to have most Galilards as storytellers. It feels as a key element to the oral tradition. However, I play up the fact that the Galilards who do a special show out of everything, by presenting it through song, dance, arts, puppets tend to be very popular among the Garou as &quot;something special&quot;. So having things in verse or presented with arts is not mandatory to the core Galilard experience, but it could give it more legitimacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}